  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If three distinct numbers <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi></math> are in G.P. and the equations <math><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> have a common root, then which one of the following statements is correct?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hfcP8",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> are in A.P.",
      "isCorrect": true,
